==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|seewey}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sǣweġ||a sea-way, a path through the sea}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|sea|way}}. Compare {{cog|de|Seegang||seaway}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|iːweɪ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} a [[lane]] or [[route]] at [[sea]] that is [[regularly]] used by [[ship]]s; a [[sea lane]] or [[trade route]]
# {{lb|en|nautical}} an [[inland]] [[waterway]] used by [[seagoing]] [[shipping]]
# {{lb|en|nautical}} the [[headway]] of a [[vessel]]

